<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1798">1798</a>–<a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera was a Colombian general who served four times as president. After leading a liberal rebellion in the civil war of 1860–1862, he oversaw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rionegro">Rionegro</a> constitution of 1863, which created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Colombia as a loose federation. He also confiscated church property and expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>.</p></div>
